    "editorial:Content_hi.txt": {
      "fingerprint": "48c835969a9742fc1f1a21a7852be348d45ca3d70c4f482fe0aecd837baf087c",
      "kind": "editorial",
      "status": "blocked",
      "issues": [
        "- In the Case Markers note, the list of perfect/imperfect past forms (खाया है, खाया था, गया है, गया था) includes intransitive verbs while stating the rule for transitive verbs → The list should only contain transitive verb forms (e.g., खाया है, खाया था) or clarify that intransitive verbs do not take ने.",
        "- In the Word Order section, the example \"मेज पर पुस्तक लाल है → लाल पुस्तक मेज पर है\" claims \"अर्थ अपरिवर्तित\" but the meaning changes from predicative to attributive → Remove the claim or use an example where the adjective is attributive in both.",
        "- In the Pronoun-Antecedent Agreement table, the corrected sentence \"सीता अपने भाई को बुलाई\" remains ungrammatical (verb should agree with masculine object → बुलाया, and ने is missing) → The corrected sentence should be \"सीता ने अपने भाई को बुलाया\" or at least \"सीता अपने भाई को बुलाया\".",
        "- In Worked Example 5, the sentence \"सीता अपना पुस्तक लाई\" lacks ने for transitive simple past, introducing a second error besides the pronoun → The sentence should be \"सीता ने अपनी पुस्तक लाई\" to isolate the pronoun error."
      ],
